<title>FRANCE: Tietmeyer says happy to retire in 1999 - report.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer says happy to retire in 1999 - report.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer would happily retire in 1999 if the European Central Bank comes into existence at that time, the International Herald Tribune reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;I only want to cast one vote, and then I will leave,&quot; the paper quoted Tietmeyer as saying. &quot;Even today, I have only a single vote in Bundesbank decisions. But I can tell you that until now I have never been outvoted.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
